  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green and decent jobs for youth (WeWork -EU)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Green and decent jobs for youth (WeWork -EU) - Via three components nationwide, the Action Sustainable Business for Uganda (SB4U) 1.0 focuses on three of the SB4U TEI pillars for policy dialogue and support: i) Trade and Sanitary and Phytosanitary Measures (SPS); ii) Governance and accountability; and (iii) Skills for decent jobs; iii). The overall objective of the Action is to contribute to sustainable economic growth and decent job creation in Uganda. A first component aims to enhance Uganda&#xbf;s capacity to comply with SPS requirements for horticulture exports to Europe, hence increasing quality and quantity of exports by companies based in Uganda to Europe. A second component aims to ensure that private sector development benefits ordinary people by enhancing human rights compliance by businesses operating in Uganda. A third component, &#xbf;Skilling and job creation&#xbf;, focuses on increasing the supply of qualified workers, and the employability of youth and creating job opportunities.&amp;nbsp;</narrative>
  </description>
